Summary:
Today’s work focused on implementing the evaluation controller to handle the core logic of the application. I created the evaluateController.js file to fetch data from GitHub and process it for portfolio evaluation. This controller acts as a bridge between incoming requests and the evaluation logic. It ensures that the data flow is properly managed and prepared for further analysis.

Outcomes:
Through this task, I gained hands-on experience in building controllers and managing application logic in a structured way. I improved my understanding of integrating external APIs, specifically fetching data from GitHub. This implementation strengthens the backend architecture by separating concerns between routes and controllers. Overall, it sets a strong foundation for adding detailed evaluation and scoring mechanisms in the project.
